 "manifest": {
  "_id": "@amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp",
  "_rev": "38-0681fe00db5e191b97a7fb95d49b7e1e",
  "description": "vibed MCP server \u2014 make it vibed from any MCP client (Codex, Cursor, Gemini, \u2026): check, login, and publish tools",
  "dist-tags": {
   "latest": "0.22.0"
  },
  "license": "MIT",
  "maintainers": [
   {
    "email": "[redacted-email:322ad8a6af53]",
    "name": "amirhosseinnateghi"
   }
  ],
  "name": "@amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp",
  "readme": "# @amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp \u2014 vibed MCP server\n\nThe **universal** vibed connector: a Model Context Protocol server that lets any\nMCP client (Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Claude Desktop, \u2026) \"make it vibed\" as\nnative tools \u2014 no per-platform skill, no shelling out.\n\nIt reuses the exact engine of the [`vibed` CLI](../cli), so the \"vibeable\" rules\nand publish behavior never diverge. Zero runtime dependencies (the MCP stdio\nprotocol is implemented directly and the engine is bundled), so `npx @amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp`\nneeds no install.\n\n## Tools\n\nAll ten, in the order the server registers them\n([`src/protocol.ts`](src/protocol.ts) is the authority \u2014 it holds the tool\ncatalog and the JSON-RPC dispatcher, while [`src/index.ts`](src/index.ts) is\njust the stdio transport, so the contract can be tested without stdin):\n\n| Tool | What it does | Key params |\n|---|---|---|\n| `vibed_storage_guide` | Prints the persistence primer. A vibe is one sandboxed file \u2014 `localStorage`/`indexedDB`/cookies and backend calls are **blocked** \u2014 so saves, leaderboards, votes and shared state go through the injected `window.vibed.storage` SDK (`local` = per-viewer, `shared` = per-post). Call it before writing any save feature, or when `vibed_check` warns `BROWSER_STORAGE`. | \u2014 |\n| `vibed_remix_guide` | Prints the remix-friendly authoring rules \u2014 one `CONFIG` block at the top, data separated from logic, plain code, and one English `STRINGS` dictionary read through `t()` (what makes a vibe auto-translatable). Call it **before** writing a vibe. | \u2014 |\n| `vibed_ideas` | The platform's idea pool: a label plus a ready-to-use prompt per idea, each guaranteed to fit the sandbox. Show the labels and let the user pick. | `about` (needs sign-in), `count` (1\u201312, default 6), `lang` (any shipped locale, default `en`) |\n| `vibed_check` | Bundle + validate against the sandbox rules (read-only, no auth). Also refuses a file that can't be **remixed** (minified, no `CONFIG`) or **translated** (no `STRINGS`/`t()`, non-English text). Every finding prints its fix \u2014 apply them to the source and re-run until it passes. | `path`, `entry`, `build` |\n| `vibed_whoami` | Is this machine signed in, and as whom? | `api` |\n| `vibed_login` | Start browser-approved device login; returns the approve URL + code. Never ask the user for a password or token. | `api` |\n| `vibed_login_wait` | Block until the user approves the pending login; saves the token. | \u2014 |\n| `vibed_draft` | **The default for \"make it vibed\"**: bundle + upload a PRIVATE draft and return a hosted sandboxed preview link (`\u2026/p/<id>/`) plus a `draftKey`. Publishes nothing \u2014 it's in no feed, profile, or search. Give the user the link and stop. Requires sign-in; refused while `vibed_check` reports blockers. | `path`, `entry`, `build`, `api` |\n| `vibed_publish` | Make a draft **public**. Only after the user explicitly says to publish \u2014 \"make it vibed\" and \"looks good\" are not publish instructions. Pass `draftKey` to promote the previewed draft (preferred); passing `path` bundles + publishes in one shot and **skips** the preview. | `draftKey`, `path`, `title`, `tags`, `unlisted`, `remixable`, `entry`, `build`, `api` |\n| `vibed_delete` | Delete one of your posts by experience id or `\u2026/e/<id>` URL. Owner-only, destructive \u2014 confirm the specific post first. | `target` (required), `api` |\n\n`vibed_publish`'s `tags` is a real enum in the tool schema: `maxItems: MAX_TAGS`\n(**5**) over the curated `TAGS` set \u2014 `game, puzzle, quiz, simulation, music,\nart, animation, story, travel, invitation, love, fun, food, sports, education,\nscience, news, tool`. Both constants are imported from\n[`@amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-cli/lib`](../cli/src/lib.ts) (which re-exports\n`@vibed/shared`), so the enum can't drift from the platform's taxonomy. There is\n**no `caption`** and **no `category`** parameter \u2014 tags replaced the category.\n\n## Configure your client\n\nThe server runs over stdio. Point your client at `npx -y @amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp@latest`.\n\n**Codex** \u2014 `~/.codex/config.toml`:\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.vibed]\ncommand = \"npx\"\nargs = [\"-y\", \"@amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp@latest\"]\n```\n\n**Cursor** \u2014 `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (or project `.cursor/mcp.json`):\n```json\n{ \"mcpServers\": { \"vibed\": { \"command\": \"npx\", \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp@latest\"] } } }\n```\n\n**Gemini CLI** \u2014 `~/.gemini/settings.json`:\n```json\n{ \"mcpServers\": { \"vibed\": { \"command\": \"npx\", \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp@latest\"] } } }\n```\n\n**Claude Code** (the plugin is the primary path, but MCP works too):\n```bash\nclaude mcp add vibed -- npx -y @amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp@latest\n```\n\nFor a local/self-hosted vibed, set the API base via env in the same config, e.g.\n`env = { VIBED_API = \"http://localhost:3200\" }` (TOML) or\n`\"env\": { \"VIBED_API\": \"http://localhost:3200\" }` (JSON).\n\nThe same config is where you turn crash reporting off \u2014 `VIBED_NO_TELEMETRY=1`\n(or `DO_NOT_TRACK=1`). When a tool call throws, the server answers the client\nfirst and then reports the crash; nothing is sent otherwise, and paths and\ncredentials are stripped before it leaves the machine. See\n[docs/connector.md](../../docs/connector.md#crash-reporting-and-how-to-turn-it-off).\n\n## Dev\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter @amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp build     # \u2192 dist/index.js (bundled, standalone)\npnpm --filter @amirhosseinnateghi/vibed-mcp dev       # run from source over stdio\n```\n\nSee [docs/connector.md](../../docs/connector.md) for the full picture.\n\n### Generic multiplayer\n\nCall `vibed_multiplayer_guide` before building remote turn-based games.\n`vibed_multiplayer_example` returns the tested self-contained Ludo source.\nGuests can play without login; all game rules stay in the vibe.\n\n## Public and private multiplayer examples\n\nBoth Ludo and Backgammon offer Public play, Create private and Join with code.\nPublic entry uses `joinAvailable({capacity})`; private creation uses\n`createRoom({capacity})`, and `joinRoom()` asks for the code through the host.\nPrivate rooms are excluded from public allocation. The examples automatically\nready private participants and let only the host call `start()` once full, so\nplayers need no extra Ready/Start step. `snapshot.visibility` restores the mode\nafter reload. A code grants entry to anyone holding it; it is not an allowlist.\n\nGet complete examples with `vibed multiplayer --example --game ludo` or\n`--game backgammon`. MCP exposes `vibed_multiplayer_example({game:\"ludo\"})` and\n`vibed_multiplayer_example({game:\"backgammon\"})`. The plugin includes both HTML\nfiles under `skills/make-it-vibed/assets/`. Both use the same generic library;\ngame rules, dice and moves remain in the examples.\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
  "time": {
